---
description: EF Core entity configs, schemas, and migrations
globs: SET.DAL/**/*.cs,SET.Shared/Models/**/*.cs
alwaysApply: false
---

# EF / data layer

- New tables: add entity in `SET.Shared/Models`, `IEntityTypeConfiguration<>` in `EntityConfigurations`, `DbSet<>` + `ApplyConfiguration` in `AppDbContext`
- Always set schema via `Schemas.*` (`app`, `goal`, `hbt`, `arlf`, `tsk`) — do not invent ad-hoc schema names
- Mirror existing config style: required/max length, defaults, FKs, cascade behavior
- For sequence-backed PKs: add `HasSequence` in `OnModelCreating` and `HasDefaultValueSql(nextval(...))` on the config
- Migrations: add under `SET.DAL/Migrations` with Designer + update `AppDbContextModelSnapshot`; name like `yyyyMMddHHmmss_Description`
- Prefer `dotnet ef migrations add` from solution root with `--project SET.DAL --startup-project SET.WebAPI`
- Child collections owned by a parent (e.g. task subtasks) should cascade delete unless product says otherwise
